cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SpecRead: A Benchmark for Specification Comprehension in Hardware Design"
message: "If you use SpecRead, please cite this dataset."
type: dataset
version: 2.1
authors:
  - family-names: Huang
    given-names: Feilian
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-2214-0233"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/EDGAhab/specread"
abstract: >-
  SpecRead is a 385-question benchmark that measures whether large language
  models understand hardware design specifications, independently of their
  RTL-generation skill. Four task types: exact retrieval, cross-section
  reasoning, mutated-spec contradiction detection, and spec-RTL consistency.
  The 98 spec-RTL items are backed by Icarus Verilog simulation harnesses
  proving each injected RTL mutation changes observable behavior. Built on
  the open-source OpenTitan project (Apache-2.0).
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - large language models
  - hardware design
  - specification comprehension
  - EDA
  - OpenTitan
